<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajah Matanda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ache</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajah Matanda, born Ache, was a ruler of Maynila, the Muslim port kingdom on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, with close ties to the Brunei court. As a young commander of a Bruneian fleet he met the survivors of Magellan's expedition in 1521. He later shared power with his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman">Rajah Sulayman</a> and died in 1572, after the Spanish occupied Manila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajah-matanda.jpg" alt="Rajah Matanda" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boxer Codex · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_old_Tagalog_king_or_noble_illustrated_in_the_1590s_Manila_manuscript,_cropped_portrait.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
